Update Manager
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "chap:Update-Manager"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With the update manager of the Eclipse platform plugins can be installed, updated and removed:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Help > Install New Software...
\series default
 installs plugins from an update site (select a site in 
\series bold
Work with
\series default
, then the plugins).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Help > Check for Updates
\series default
 updates the installed plugins.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Help > About Bio7 > Installation Details
\series default
 lists the installed software: plugins can be uninstalled and the 
\series bold
Installation History
\series default
 reverts the installation to an earlier state (e.g., after a corrupted installation).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Preferences > Install/Update > Available Software Sites
\series default
 manages the update sites.
\end_layout

